+              <p class="state-note"><span class="lbl">Shipped in 0.15.0</span><code>HeatLedger</code> and <code>CrimeRecord</code> (cops-n-crooks <code>wanted/heat/</code>), fed by <code>HeatListener</code>. <code>HeatWantedTracker</code> replaces the deleted <code>KillComboWantedTracker</code>, is always installed and reads Heat.Enable on every call. The knobs live in <code>npc/wanted.yml</code> in the module jar, not settings.yml: <code>Wanted.Heat.Enable</code> true, Star_Thresholds [100, 250, 450, 700, 1000], Streak_Bonus 1.5, Seen_By_Cop_Multiplier 1.5, Turf_War_Multiplier 0.5, Assault_Repeat_Seconds 10, and the crime weights in the sketch above (merged key by key over the defaults). Crimes published in 0.15: Kill_Player, Kill_Civilian, Kill_Cop, Assault_Cop (once per attacker and cop every 10 s) and Resisting_Arrest (breaking free). The other seven weights ship in the file but nothing publishes them until later releases. A civilian kill goes through the ledger and counts once. Exempt, with heat on or off: a self-defence kill (the victim hit the killer first in that fight, a fixed 30 s window, PvP only, no config key; a simpler form of the 0.16 self-defence rules) and a player kill while defending your own contested turf (<code>WantedKillTracker.exemptsKill</code>, inert until the gang module loads; this is Gang &amp; Turf P6.4, which now only needs a check). Cop and civilian kills inside a contested turf keep full heat. A kill at max stars adds no auto bounty, and a self-kill claims nothing. Heat.Enable false restores the old combo math. Deviations: with heat on there is no combo object, so an outside <code>KillComboEvent</code> listener hears nothing on the default config (<code>CrimeCommittedEvent</code> is the public signal), and a one-shot cop kill is Assault_Cop plus Kill_Cop, two stars (an open owner question).<span class="ref"><code>HeatLedgerTest</code> (14), <code>HeatWantedTrackerTest</code> (14, incl. <code>defenderKillInsideOwnContestedTurf_commit